  "description": "A good Greek salad must be made with peak summer tomatoes, crisp and refreshing cucumbers, briny black olives, and just a bit of onion, here quickly pickled to tame its pungency and add pops of acidity to each slice. Then the ultimate topper: slabs of feta.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: pitted Kalamata olives → briny black olives; Kosher salt → sea salt; dried Greek oregano → Mediterranean oregano\n\nNotes: Pit-in olives are often better-quality than pre-pitted ones; we recommend buying pit-in olives and removing the pits yourself.",
